  "text": "(See GMC § 13.30.100)\nStormwater Quality Permit\nStormwater Quality Permit Renewal\nStormwater Quality Permit reinspection fee\n$350.00 for initial permit\nand SWMP review\n$125.00 for annual\nrenewal\n$40.00\nThe following fee schedule shall be applicable to water sample analysis\nperformed by personnel from the Environmental Services Division. Said\nfees shall be paid upon completion of analysis. Fees shall be cumulative\nwhere multiple samples are analyzed. These fees do not apply to Golden\nresidents requesting analysis of potable water delivered by the City of\nGolden.\nTotal Organic Carbon\nColiform: presence/absence with E. coli elimination/confirmation if\npositive\n$40.00\n$25.00\nUTILITIES/ENGINEERING/CONSTRUCTION FEE SCHEDULE\nAdditional Fees (See GMC § 13.04.145)\nFor administration, inspection, publication of\nnotice, cost of protessional consultants,\nincluding legal review\nFee\nActual Cost\nDeposit Required 5\n$1,000.00\nDrainage Service Fees\nCommercial and Multi-Family Accounts more\nthan four units\nSingle-Family Residential and Multi-Family\nResidential with less than four units\nFire Hydrant Permit Temporary Water Service\nDamage deposit at time of issuance\nMeter rental fee\n*Take full responsibility for any repairs to\ndamaged City property\nFloodplain Development Permit\nAny Improvement >50% Structure Value\nBuilding Footprint Expansion\n$.00386/square foot impervious area\n$11.75 per unit\n$500.00\n$1,000.00 per six months\n$200.00\n$100.00\n5 For deposits, applicant is required to enter into a consultant reimbursement agreement and submit the\napplication deposit fee in addition to the nonrefundable application fee.\n25",
